      "id": "a4b6e24b-495c-4468-a721-844e4d6986ef",
      "body": "Here are the X-class flares in 2012 from `data/hek_flare_catalog.csv`:\n\n| start_time | peak_time | GOES_class | AR |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2012-01-27T17:37 | 18:37 | X1.7 | 11402 |\n| 2012-03-05T02:30 | 04:09 | X1.1 | 11429 |\n| 2012-03-07T00:02 | 00:24 | X5.4 | 11429 |\n| 2012-03-07T01:05 | 01:14 | X1.3 | 11430 |\n| 2012-07-06T23:01 | 23:08 | X1.1 | 11515 |\n| 2012-07-12T15:37 | 16:49 | X1.4 | 11520 |\n| 2012-10-23T03:13 | 03:17 | X1.8 | 11598 |\n\nThe awk one-liner (from `flare_forecast/` dir):\n```bash\nawk -F, 'NR==1 || ($4 ~ /^X/ && $1 ~ /^2012/)' data/hek_flare_catalog.csv\n```\n\nThe two March 2012 events (X5.4, X1.3) are back-to-back \u2014 worth checking if that's what `getitem(0)` is showing you in the notebook.",
